<article class="env-lemma" id="0HAD">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0HAD">Lemma <span data-tag="0HAD">29.20.7</span>.</a> The following types of schemes are excellent. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
Any scheme locally of finite type over a field. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Any scheme locally of finite type over a Noetherian complete local ring. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Any scheme locally of finite type over $\mathbf{Z}$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Any scheme locally of finite type over a Dedekind ring of characteristic zero. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemmas <a href="/tag/0HAB" data-tag="0HAB">29.20.5</a> and <a href="/tag/0HAC" data-tag="0HAC">29.20.6</a> we only need to show that the rings mentioned above are excellent. For this see More on Algebra, Proposition <a href="/tag/07QW" data-tag="07QW">15.53.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>